    "text_full": "Solutions\nTools\nIntegrations\nResources\nPricing\nGet a demo\nLogin\nRegister\nNO SPREADSHEETS. NO SELLER CENTRAL.\nTrack listing status and true cost across every SKU\n\nAll seller SKUs in one place — synced from Amazon and created through Lister. Status, cost breakdown, and listing history visible per SKU without opening Seller Central.\n\nGet Started\nHOW IT WORKS\nStatus, cost, and history — in one SKU table\n\nOne table. Updated as you list, order, and ship.\n\n1\nSee your full SKU inventory\n\nSKUs synced from Amazon and created through Lister all appear together. Channel, listing status, and landed cost visible per row at a glance.\n\n2\nFilter by status or cost source\n\nSwitch between active, inactive, pending, and error. Filter by cost source to see which SKUs have costs from a PO, weighted, or overridden.\n\n3\nManage landed cost\n\nClick the cost to open the breakdown. See unit cost, PO expenses, prep fees, and inbound costs, with overrides available.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nIncomplete SKU data is an invisible cost\n\nLanded cost gaps, missing SKU history, and inactive listings all affect what you actually make per unit. None of them surface unless you look.\n\nCOST ACCURACY\nActual cost from your own data\n\nLanded cost traces back to the purchase order the SKU was created from. If the SKU appeared in multiple orders, cost is a weighted average across all of them. FBA inbound fees from shipments are included automatically.\n\nSKU HISTORY\nFull SKU history, one tab away\n\nOne product can accumulate multiple SKUs over time. Open any product record and the SKUs tab shows every seller SKU attached to it — status, landed cost, and creation date.\n\nNO DUPLICATE ENTRIES\nExisting SKUs, ready when you list\n\nWhen listing a product you have sold before, the SKU already exists. Pick it from the table instead of creating a new one. Your cost history, status, and identifiers stay intact — no lost data.\n\nWHAT'S INCLUDED\nEverything the SKU database handles\n\nThe details that matter when you are managing active inventory across multiple seller SKUs.\n\nAmazon sync\n\nAll seller SKUs sync automatically from your connected Amazon account\n\nStatus filtering\n\nSwitch between active, inactive, pending, draft, and error\n\nError visibility\n\nFailure reason shown on hover for every error-status SKU\n\nLanded cost breakdown\n\nUnit cost, PO expenses, prep, and inbound fees per SKU\n\nCost overrides\n\nManually adjust any landed cost component when needed\n\nPer-product SKU view\n\nAll seller SKUs for a product visible from the product record\n\nWORKFLOW\nSKUs trace back to listings, orders, and shipments\n\nEvery seller SKU moves through your workflow — from sourced product to live listing. These are the tools it connects to.\n\nList\nLister\n\nSeller SKUs created through Lister appear in the SKUs table immediately\n\nList\nFBA Shipments\n\nInbound fees from shipments flow into landed cost automatically\n\nSource\nPurchase Orders\n\nUnit cost and order expenses pull from linked POs into landed cost\n\nSource\nProducts\n\nEvery seller SKU linked to a product is visible from the product record\n\nCOMPLETE YOUR WORKFLOW\nSourcing decisions behind every SKU start at research\n\nThe margin each SKU generates starts with the research decisions made before it was ever listed.\n\nPrice List Analyzer\n\nTurn a supplier catalog into a shortlist of profitable products.\n\nAnalyze\nRestriction Checker\n\nConfirm you can sell every product before it reaches a listing.\n\nAnalyze\nBrand Analyzer\n\nSee brand revenue, BSR, and Buy Box share before committing to a supplier.\n\nDiscover\nBrowser Extension\n\nCheck margins and restrictions on any Amazon product page.\n\nDiscover\nFrequently Asked Questions\nVisit Help Center\nWhat is the SKUs database?\nHow are SKUs synced from Amazon?\nHow is landed cost calculated?\nCan I override landed cost manually?\nHow do I see all SKUs for a product?\nWhat listing statuses are shown?\nYour SKU data is already there\n\nEvery SKU created through Lister, every cost from a PO, every inbound fee from a shipment — all visible in one table.\n\nGet Started\n\nNot sure which plan fits your sourcing workflow? Chat with our team — we're happy to help.\n\nNAVIGATION\nHome\nPricing\nDownload\nSOLUTIONS\nOnline Arbitrage\nWholesale\nDropshipping\nAgencies\nPRODUCTS\nPrice List Analyzer\nLister\nPurchase Orders\nSuppliers\nWarehouses\nSeller Assistant Extension\nIP-Alert by Seller Assistant\nVPN by Seller Assistant\nBulk Restriction Checker\nSeller Spy\nBrand Analyzer\nFREE TOOLS\nASIN Lookup\nIP-Alert Lookup\nSupplier Finder\nASIN to UPC\nUPC to ASIN\nEAN to ASIN\nFEATURES\nFBM & FBA Calculator\nVAT Calculator\nAmazon IP-Alert\nSide Panel View\nAmazon Quick View\nStorefront Widget\nAlerts & Flags\nRestrictions Checker\nSales Estimator\nOffers\nVariation Viewer\nStock Checker\nASIN Grabber\nSub-Accounts for VAs\nExport to Google Sheets\nNotes\nALTERNATIVES\nAnalyzer.Tools Alternative\nScan Unlimited Alternative\nSmartScout Alternative\nRevSeller Alternative\nBuyBotPro Alternative\nAZInsight Alternative\nSellerAmp Alternative\nIP-Alert Alternative\nDS Quick View Alternative\nPARTNERS\nAffiliate Program\nPartners\nAmazon Experts\nPress Kit\nRESOURCES\nBlog\nGet a Demo\nHelp Center\nOffice Hours\nNews & Updates\nProduct Roadmap\nReviews\nINTEGRATIONS\nZapier\nMake\nAirtable\nn8n\nGoogle Sheets\nSeller Central\nPrep Centers\nAPI\nOTHER LINKS\nIP-Alert by Seller Assistant\nLANGUAGE\n🇬🇧 English\n🇷🇺 Русский\n🇪🇸 Español\n🇹🇷 Türkçe\n\nCopyright © 2019-2026 Linen Art, LLC. All rights reserved.\nAmazon and all related marks are trademarks of Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates.\n\nTerms of Use\n|\nPrivacy Policy\n|\nCookie Policy\n|\nRefund Policy"
